  "question": {
    "text": "In the ground state of atomic <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>26</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, the spin-only magnetic moment is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>BM</mi></math>. (Round off to the Nearest Integer).<br />[ Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>:</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>73</mn><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>41</mn><mo>]</mo></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "49",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Ar</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ae4a1338-7d6d-4210-8759-e4bdc5872c1b-image.png\" style=\"width: 224px; height: 62px;\" /></p><p>Number of unpaired <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>24</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>89</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math></p><p>Nearest integer value will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>49</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
